# The knowledge index, lock and every promoted experience are generated files, and the scripts
# write them with LF. A Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true hands the working tree CRLF
# instead, so the next regeneration rewrites the same content with LF and git reports a change
# that `git diff` shows as zero changed lines. That is a line-ending artifact, not stale content,
# and it makes the "generated files are committed" check impossible to pass on a Windows runner.
# Pin the checkout to what the generator writes.
*.json text eol=lf
